---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { AUTHOR_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, LEGAL, SITE_NAMES, SITE_URL } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { displayDate } from '../../lib/format';
import { P } from '../../lib/engine/params';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title={`Editorial policy – ${SITE_NAMES[lang]}`} description="How Precio Luz Real checks prices and taxes: official sources only, a date for every value, automated tests and corrections that show on every page at once." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Editorial policy' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Editorial policy</h1>
    <h2>Sources</h2><p>Primary sources only: Red Eléctrica for prices, the BOE for tolls (CNMC), charges (Ministry), taxes and the social discount, and the INE for the price index that triggers tax cuts. A blog, a comparison site or a retailer’s page is never a source. Each value sits in the parameter file with its rule and the date it was read ({P.retrieved_at}).</p>
    <h2>What we do not publish</h2><p>A value we could not read in an official source is not published, which is why we do not calculate Ceuta and Melilla. A day’s price that Red Eléctrica has not published is never shown as real: it appears as an estimated average, with a notice. We rank no retailers and take no money to mention anyone.</p>
    <h2>Checks</h2><p>The engine is tested on every release with hand-worked cases and with every hour of the year, whose tolls and charges must match the BOE. Parameters are reviewed every 1 January and whenever a new rule on the tariff or its taxes is published.</p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2><p>Errors are fixed as soon as confirmed. Write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. More in <a href={route('method', lang)}>method and sources</a> and <a href={route('about', lang)}>about us</a>.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
